{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"paramount-ducal-snake","bridge_project":"","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nThe project Jira target is Jira Cloud (`https://navasage.atlassian.net`), while `reconciler.rich_text_cutover` defaults to `off`. Enable the already-shipped Markdown↔ADF bridge behavior for this project without enabling the unrelated Data Center wire.\n\n## Plan\n- Add a `[reconciler]` table to the project `rebar.toml`.\n- Set `rich_text_cutover = \"cloud\"`.\n- Validate the project configuration and confirm the resolved value is sourced from `rebar.toml`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `rebar.toml` configures `reconciler.rich_text_cutover` as `cloud`.\n- [ ] `rebar config validate` accepts the updated configuration.\n- [ ] The resolved configuration reports the rich-text cutover as `cloud` from the project config.","id":"52bf-bc40-3fcb-4729","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["configuration","jira","rich-text"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Enable Jira Cloud rich-text reconciliation for rebar"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787004892545062001,"uuid":"6eaea2db-36b7-4668-afbc-49c0f50d32de"}